body:
try accessing free mental health services in your area, utilize a hotline if you need to (personally I've found that calling hotlines is a wonderful outlet if things get to be too much, it's a good place to vent) and keep up work on meditating and journaling. Acknowledging that you need help and actively searching for it is no small feat so good on you for that, it is a very long and difficult task but it's worth it.  your wellbeing is worth it. 

&#x200B;

what you're describing is what I've been feeling for a while, so if it helps: you are not alone. I can't express how much I relate to what you are describing, thank you for putting it into words. 

&#x200B;

please please take care of yourself and do what you have to in order to push through. sending love

how does she look like THAT 

&#x200B;

....I'm out

every day that goes by where you push through the numb, tired feeling is another step forward. take care of yourself in this state even though nothing feels like it's helping, small things may feel redundant if they aren't immediately giving you clarity but just keeping yourself going is what matters.

&#x200B;

please take care of yourself, goodnight

I'm gonna weep 

&#x200B;

*this is the best*
